@startuml Authentication Flow

skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam maxMessageSize 200

skinparam participant {
  BackgroundColor AliceBlue
  BorderColor SteelBlue
  FontStyle bold
}
skinparam actor {
  BackgroundColor White
  BorderColor DarkSlateGray
}
skinparam database {
  BackgroundColor LemonChiffon
  BorderColor Goldenrod
}
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor DarkSlateGray
  LifeLineBorderColor SteelBlue
  GroupBorderColor Gray
  GroupBackgroundColor WhiteSmoke
  DividerBackgroundColor LightSteelBlue
  DividerFontStyle bold
  SeparatorBackgroundColor LightGray
  SeparatorFontStyle bold
  NoteBackgroundColor Cornsilk
  NoteBorderColor Goldenrod
}

title Authentication Flow\n<size:11>Traefik ForwardAuth  ·  JWT HS256  ·  auth-service</size>

actor       "Client"                        as client
participant "Traefik\n(API Gateway)"        as gw
participant "auth-service\nHTTP :8000"      as auth
database    "Auth DB\n(PostgreSQL)"         as db
participant "Target Service\n(e.g. course-service)" as svc

' ─────────────────────────────────────
== 1. Login — obtain tokens ==
' ─────────────────────────────────────

autonumber 1

client  ->  gw   : POST /auth/login\n{ email, password, portal_id }
note right of gw : Public route — no middleware.\nTraefik forwards as-is.
gw      ->  auth : POST /auth/login

auth    ->  db   : SELECT * FROM auth\nWHERE login = email AND portal_id = portal_id
db      --> auth : user record\n(user_id, password_hash, role, portal_id)

auth    ->  auth : bcrypt.CompareHashAndPassword\n(password_hash, password)

alt #FFE4E4 invalid credentials
  auth  --> gw   : 401 Unauthorized
  gw    --> client : 401 Unauthorized
else #E4FFE4 valid credentials
  auth  ->  auth : GenerateToken(user_id, login, portal_id, role)\nHS256 · TTL = config.jwt.expiration
  auth  ->  auth : GenerateToken(refresh)\nHS256 · TTL = 24 h

  auth  ->  db   : INSERT INTO auth_logs\n(user_id, login, action="LOGIN_SUCCESS", ip)

  auth  --> gw   : 200 OK\n{ access_token, refresh_token }
  gw    --> client : 200 OK\n{ access_token, refresh_token }
end

' ─────────────────────────────────────
== 2. Protected request — happy path ==
' ─────────────────────────────────────

autonumber 10

client  ->  gw   : GET /courses\nAuthorization: Bearer <access_token>

note right of gw
  Route matched → **user-auth** middleware fires.
  Traefik issues a ForwardAuth sub-request
  to auth-service before forwarding the original.
end note

gw      ->  auth : GET /auth\nAuthorization: Bearer <access_token>\n<size:9>(Traefik ForwardAuth sub-request)</size>

auth    ->  auth : jwt.ParseWithClaims(token, secret)\n— verify HS256 signature\n— verify exp claim

alt #FFE4E4 token invalid / expired / missing
  auth  --> gw   : 401 Unauthorized
  gw    --> client : 401 Unauthorized\n<size:9>(original request dropped)</size>
else #E4FFE4 token valid
  auth  --> gw   : 200 OK\nX-Auth-User-ID: <user_id>\nX-Auth-User-Login: <login>

  note right of gw
    Traefik copies **authResponseHeaders**
    (X-Auth-User-ID, X-Auth-User-Login)
    into the original request headers,
    then forwards to the target service.
  end note

  gw    ->  svc  : GET /courses\nX-Auth-User-ID: <user_id>\nX-Auth-User-Login: <login>

  svc   ->  svc  : handle request\nusing user context from headers

  svc   --> gw   : 200 OK · { ...payload }
  gw    --> client : 200 OK · { ...payload }
end

@enduml
